  "notes": "Drum-forward British producer working through vintage consoles and live tracking. The drum claim is the model: \"the identity is percussion as architecture — martial beats, stomps, hand-claps and a played kit tracked in a live room, entering as a structural event rather than running throughout.\" So the kick is a four-square martial pulse, the snare stack is `clap` alone with the widest human offset here under a `large` room tail, `hihat.continuous` is false at `fillDensity` 0.04 with the roll vocabulary off, and `tomLow`, `tom` and `tambourine` carry the stomps at a forward gain. The humanize block is a played one; \"a 72-channel vintage EMI Neve in one room and an SSL in the other, i.e. a hybrid analogue/digital chain\" is the wide velocity spread. Harmony is his most specific researched fact and it is authored as the voicing rather than as a numeral: \"minor keys with open-fifth (power-chord) voicings in place of full triads — documented on his best-known production as i5—v5—VII5 — plus natural-minor VI—VII motion and gospel plagal cadences.\" A fifth is a triad with the third removed, so `triad` sits at 0.86 (the highest in this section) with almost no extension, the voicing is `open` and wide, and the families are the i—v—VII and VI—VII sets the source names. No `bass808` block: \"no 808. Electric bass and doubled low piano; the harmonic floor is often bare fifths, which is why his records sound wide and hollow before the choir enters\", which is a `mirror_kick` at 0.94 with root-fifth cells and no passing motion. \"Massed chanting backing vocals are his standard countermelody\" is `sustain_pad`; the arrangement is the documented additive terracing, claps then kit then choir, with an abrupt full stop. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because the research says \"the tempo band is aggregated\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers and `bpm.mode` 105 (the midpoint of the stated 70—140 band) are INFERRED.",
